(376, 'Laurianne', 'donate@givenlife.org.uk', 'Nigeria Christins are bleeding!!!', 'Nigeria Christins are bleeding!!!.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe implore your support to rescue the victimised Christians in Nigeria.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOur foundation is working with the locals to sake financial and resources support from the general public from across the world. Our team that provides holistic care, focusing on physical, psychological, social, and spiritual need.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe need<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. Food to feed the over one million internally displaced people (IDP) in the various camps. As of November 2024, DTM statistics identified a total of 1,322,766 IDPs in 225,458 households across 10-11 states in Nigeria out of the total 36 states of Nigeria and Abuja. <br />\r\nRead the news: https://dtm.iom.int/sites/g/files/tmzbdl1461/files/reports/Nigeria%20-20ATLAS%20-20R16202025_.pdf?iframe=true<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFood stuffs are highly expensive in Nigeria and the regime of the current Nigerian government monopolized the few importers that imports grains and fruits to Nigeria, keep majority in abject poverty due to lack of competion. With over 20.12% inflation in August 2025, over 139 million good people of Nigeria has been thrown into abject poverty.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2.<br />\r\nShelter and sleeping (Tents, tarpaulins, and ropes Blankets, sleeping mats, and sleeping bags Bedding sets (sheets, pillows), Cots, non-perishables, water purification tablets, etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHygiene and health (Soap, shampoo, and toothpaste, Sanitary products and diapers, Toothbrushes and towels, Wet wipes and toilet paper, First-aid kits, Mosquito nets, etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFood and cooking (Non-perishable food items (rice, pasta, tinned food), Kitchen utensils, pots, and pans, sleeping gear, sleeping mats, Tin openers and matches, Water jugs and purification tablets, Fuel for cooking, etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTools and miscellaneous (Generators, power banks, and flashlights, Batteries, Chainsaws and wheelbarrows, Heavy-duty black bags, Clothes and shoes (new or in very good condition), Children&amp;#039;s toys, etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFinancial and other donations (Monetary donations (use official, reputable channels), Gift cards, Volunteer services, etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. We are working with some group of locals in various capacity. The locals are organizing themselves some local teachers training them with some skills with the support of some foreign foundations. After the training, they supply the skilled teachers to existing schools to improve learning quality for children of the deprived Nigerians. We finance to carry out this mission.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. We pays the children school fees on continual unlimited scholarship in the local scheme especially for children’ whose parents were killed by Islamic terrorist extremists. We need finance to carry out this mission.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. Before you send any support, please contact our lawyer in Nigeria, Advocate Okonjo Alfred Ikechukwuka Law Firm in his email id: adv@okonjoalfredikechukwuka.com.ng and inform him how much you intend to send. Afterwhich, if you intend to send less than 750 GBP, kindly send it via Money Gram or Ria Money Transfer, to:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n		Receiver Name:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n				Surname		Clark<br />\r\n				names		John Colin	<br />\r\n		City:		London or Manchester<br />\r\n		Country:	United Kingdom<br />\r\n		Amount:		???<br />\r\n		Send the payment receipt after making the payment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf you intend to send more than 750 pounds or intend to send physical packages, kindly get back to us to supply you with other mode of payment information and the courier receiver information in Nigeria.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOn behalf of Given Life, I would like to express my deepest gratitude for your kindness, generosity, and support.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSincerely,<br />\r\nLaurianne DACOSTA<br />\r\n(Director)<br />\r\nGiven Life - Manchester<br />\r\n2 Ashbury Place,<br />\r\nManchester, England, M40 8DX,<br />\r\nUnited Kingdom<br />\r\n+44 161 262 1271 (Tel)<br />\r\n+44 161 262 1272 (Fax)<br />\r\nhttps://givenlife.org.uk<br />\r\nhttps://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/14279031', '2025-11-04 08:42:12'),
